Fixes for the FaceTime plugin, @openclaw/facetime 2026.9.6 (OpenClaw, MIT).

1. Calls end. On macOS 27 the last status the helper reports after a hangup
   is 6 (disconnected), with no end date, so the plugin never saw the call
   end and refused every new call until a gateway restart. Status 6 now
   counts as ended.
2. Tool work finishes. A repeat consult from the voice with no new caller
   speech (often the voice hearing itself) cancelled the check in progress,
   so its answer never arrived. Repeats are ignored until the caller says
   something new.
3. The greeting: by name, the way a friend picks up, no self-introduction.
4. The audio driver builds with Xcode 27 (deployment target 12.0; the
   installer's pinned digest is updated to match).

Apply after every install or update of the plugin, then restart the gateway:

  cd "$(openclaw plugins inspect facetime --json | node -pe 'JSON.parse(require("fs").readFileSync(0)).plugin.rootDir')"
  patch -p1 < ~/uno/patches/facetime-2026.9.6.patch

